{"title": "Motorola is filling the gap OnePlus left behind, mostly", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/01/motorola-oneplus-gap/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/09/motorola-signature-27-1_942c71.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">As we near the launch of Motorola’s return to the flagship space, it’s becoming clear that the company is ready to fill a gap left by the departure of OnePlus, though there’s one very obvious difference between the two.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\" />\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left wp-block-paragraph\"><em>9to5Google Weekender by Ben Schoon is a part of our free newsletter that also includes ‘Inbox,’ a twice-weekly roundup of key stories from around the web by Daniel Bader. <a href=\"https://9to5google.beehiiv.com/subscribe\">Sign up here</a> to get Weekender delivered to your inbox every Sunday along with ‘Inbox’ on Tuesday and Thursday. <a href=\"https://9to5google.com/feature/newsletter/\">You can find past issues here</a>.</em></p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\" />\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/01/motorola-oneplus-gap/#more-734888\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-01T05:00:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-04T17:54:35.409444+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "Motorola Signature 27 specs detailed in new video, including Tandem OLED display", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/10/31/motorola-signature-27-specs-hands-on/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/10/motorola-signature-27-hands-on-2.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Ahead of its launch next week, a new video offers a closer look at the Motorola Signature 27 as well as confirming some key specs.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/10/31/motorola-signature-27-specs-hands-on/#more-735267\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-10-31T03:00:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-04T17:54:35.409444+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "Samsung mercilessly mocks iPhone Duo ‘crackgate’ in Galaxy Z Fold 8 ads [Video]", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/10/30/samsung-mocks-iphone-duo-crackgate-galaxy-z-fold-8/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/10/galaxy-z-fold-8-iphone-duo-crackgate.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Samsung isn’t holding back when it comes to the iPhone Duo’s messy start. In new ads, the company mocks iPhone Duo’s “crackgate” with a push for customers to buy the Galaxy Z Fold 8 instead, and there’s not an ounce of subtlety here.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/10/30/samsung-mocks-iphone-duo-crackgate-galaxy-z-fold-8/#more-735274\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-10-30T16:20:00+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-04T17:54:35.409444+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "Pixelated 123: The primary value is the clock", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/10/30/pixelated-123-the-primary-value-is-the-clock/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2024/03/Pixelated-cover.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Welcome to Pixelated episode 123. This week, Damien and Abner share their earliest impressions of the Fitbit Edge, Google’s latest fitness tracker that promises to split the difference between the Fitbit Air and the Pixel Watch 5. After, the gang gets bleak about the future of RAM prices before turning their attention to Apple one last time to ask…<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hyqxZxIBDoo\">good lord what is happening in there?</a></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Enjoy the show? You can listen to our weekly members-only Pixelated Pro bonus episode by <a href=\"https://9to5google.com/pro/\">signing up for 9to5Google Pro</a> for just $5 per month, or about $1 per episode.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Sponsored by Proton Unlimited</strong>: Pixelated listeners can save 30% on an annual subscription to the company’s suite of privacy-friendly services by <a href=\"https://proton.me/9to5google\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">signing up using our link</a>. Thanks to Proton Unlimited for sponsoring the podcast.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-audio\"><audio controls=\"controls\" src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/10/pix-123-main.mp3\"></audio></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-subscribe\">Subscribe</h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLcKP282Ii48tKK_KUt1kq1Ist9FkYR6lO\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">YouTube Podcasts</a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://pca.st/podcast/ac8e6ce0-06b1-0136-c264-7d73a919276a\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">